  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Community Responses to HIV/AIDS in Dar es Salaam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. To increase awareness of HIV/AIDS amongst young people, religious leaders, specific vulnerable groups (such as bar maids, commercial sex workers) and local government officials in the target population (3 districts of Dar es Salaam and 5 districts of the coast region).
2. To increase the number of community members who are knowledgeable and confident enough to engage in prevention activities within their communities.
3. To increase the number of active Community Health Educators (CHEs) from 77 to 230 in the first two years of the project.
4. To increase the number of skilled family care givers in the community, thereby improving the quality of care.
5. To actively involve community members in the care and support of HIV/AIDS orphans and vulnerable children.
6. To improve coordination between agencies in the Archdiocese of Dar es Salaam working at all levels, to share good practice and engage with the government health management structures on policy issues.
7. To increase awareness about gender issues and their importance in the HIV/AIDS pandemic among project staff members, CHEs and the communities in which they are working.</narrative>
  </description>
